1999
You can now do an optimization or a single-point AM1 or PM3 calc with BOSS
and the CM1 charges are written to the sum file with standard L-J parameters.

For the single-point calc, one declares AM1S or PM3S at the top of the par file
instead of AM1 or PM3 and ICALC = 2 (optimization) in the cmd file.
We normally scale the CM1A charges by 1.2 (see revision above) and the CM1P by 1.3 for
neutral moleucles. E.g., the top of the par file is

 parg41: Gas-phase optimization
 The principal solvent is
NONE
 QM method, charge calc & scale, solute charges:
PM3SCM1P 1.30  0  0  0

The single-point calculation is performed for the geometry in the zmat
file. 

Thus, with autozmat one can now quickly go
Sybyl mol2 file -> BOSS zmat file -> CM1 charges and LJ parameters

See the README file in aazmat.

**** Note there are scripts in boss/scripts that automatically handle
     these operations:

xAM1SP      - AM1 single-point calculation for a neutral system
xPM3SP      - PM3 single-point calculation for a neutral system
xAM1OPT     - AM1 optimization for a neutral system
xPM3OPT     - PM3 optimization for a neutral system
xMOLZ       - convert MDL .mol file to optimized BOSS Z-matrix file
xMOL2Z      - convert .mol2 file to optimized BOSS Z-matrix file

